  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "u10-1",
      "title": "Two nie's",
      "explanation": [
        "**nie** = not. Afrikaans usually puts **nie** twice in a negative sentence: once after the verb and once **at the very end**.",
        "**Ek praat nie Afrikaans nie.** = I don't speak Afrikaans.",
        "If **nie** is already the last word, you only need one: **Ek weet nie.** (I don't know.)",
        "**verstaan** = understand, **weet** = know.",
        "Don't! = **Moenie … nie!** → **Moenie huil nie!** (Don't cry!)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "af": "Ek verstaan nie.",
          "en": "I don't understand."
        },
        {
          "af": "Ek praat nie Afrikaans nie.",
          "en": "I don't speak Afrikaans."
        },
        {
          "af": "Sy is nie moeg nie.",
          "en": "She isn't tired."
        },
        {
          "af": "Moenie huil nie!",
          "en": "Don't cry!"
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        "nie",
        "verstaan",
        "weet",
        "moenie",
        "huil"
      ],
